# Build context filter for the Tulen image.
#
# Two jobs here. The obvious one is keeping the upload small — the raw tree is
# ~2.5 GB and all but ~2 MB of it is either regenerable or actively harmful in
# the image. The load-bearing one is the checkpoints exclusion: the Dockerfile
# downloads the weights into vendor/CountGD/checkpoints, and a later
# `COPY vendor/CountGD/` would overwrite them with whatever the dev machine had
# (or bloat the context by 1.6 GB to write identical bytes).

# --- virtualenvs -------------------------------------------------------------
# .venv (MLX/API), .venv-torch, .venv-countgd — ~700 MB each, and built for
# macOS arm64, so they are not merely redundant but unusable on linux/amd64.
.venv
.venv*

# --- python noise ------------------------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache

# --- vcs / tooling -----------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# --- model weights: fetched at build time, never shipped through context -----
# Both entries matter. The first is the 1.6 GB the Dockerfile downloads itself.
# The second is 19 MB of COCO val2017 annotations used only by CountGD's
# training/eval scripts — nothing on the inference path reads it (the sole
# reference, util/static_data_path.py, points at an unrelated absolute path).
vendor/CountGD/checkpoints
vendor/CountGD/config/instances_val2017.json

# Defensive hygiene rather than a fix for anything present today: the vendored
# clone currently carries no compiled artifacts, and CountGD's CUDA
# deformable-attention build is deliberately absent — this is a CPU image and
# models/GroundingDINO/ms_deform_attn.py falls back to its pure-PyTorch path.
# If someone ever builds those ops locally, they must not leak into the image.
**/*.whl
**/*.egg
**/build/
**/*.so

# --- things that must not become part of a deploy ----------------------------
# web/ is the superseded desktop UI; webapp/ is the one the API serves at /.
# The notebook/PDF patterns are recursive on purpose — the vendored clone
# carries a 40 KB Colab notebook and a 99 KB paper figure. vendor/CountGD's
# LICENSE is deliberately NOT excluded: it is a vendored third-party tree and
# its licence ships with it.
web
docs
README.md
**/*.ipynb
**/*.pdf

# yolo11x.pt — 114 MB of an unrelated detector this service never loads.
yolo11x.pt
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx

# --- local state -------------------------------------------------------------
# SQLite lives on the Railway volume at /data. Baking a dev database into the
# image would ship stale jobs and, worse, seed the volume with rows whose media
# files do not exist.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
.tulen
workspace
runs
out
tmp
*.log

# --- dev-only entrypoints ----------------------------------------------------
# The container has its own entrypoint; these bind 127.0.0.1 and reference the
# macOS venvs by path.
run.sh
start.sh

# --- sample media ------------------------------------------------------------
*.mp4
*.mov
*.m4v
*.webm
*.mkv
*.avi
*.srt
